<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>After floods, Nepal minister demands 'climate justice'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6982eb2bffaf4ac57472156c879fb8afee172993ba510214deca7333d1b183</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-floods-nepal-minister-demands-climate-justice/a-79372239--033ba1d032f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-floods-nepal-minister-demands-climate-justice/a-79372239?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With Nepal still reeling from the devastating floods in August, Kathmandu is calling for climate justice and seeking compensation from the UN-backed Loss and Damage Fund, Environment Minister Geeta Chaudhary told DW.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Police investigate alleged gang-rape in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d7b2b7ac75a26624a7e568fa617f767f7cd0f867a84a052c4c0c968c9ce9064</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T06:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177--41caa0443681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While India is fuming over a viral video of two minors being harassed in Bihar, a case of an alleged gang-rape of a minor has emerged in a posh Delhi neighborhood. Meanwhile, India's foreign minister is at the UNGA.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Trump-Xi summit nears, Europe is caught in middle of US-China rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45939eb17182fd7b234e2e15a738489b03ddebb70d30484a29a62e9627e6afe2</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540--3c6355b77845.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China's Xi Jinping is traveling to Washington this week. Regardless of what comes from his talks with US President Trump, the EU will likely remain stuck between erratic US trade policy and Beijing's export machine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nuclear power is back on Southeast Asia's energy agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e435a2c9c8038121bc3354d5bc1691d09cd538a7e2ed7a695bad0711ff5fae63</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744--70fdccf67ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising electricity demand, shocks in energy security and climate commitments are reviving long-stalled plans for nuclear power across Southeast Asia. But proponents of nuclear energy still face major obstacles.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's road rage: When cars become weapons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36deefa7a61c3495455551df099144b52e3a3bcffb87f0b334bb75b72469ffc1</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-road-rage-when-cars-become-weapons/a-79355073--1e7f2ce4312e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-road-rage-when-cars-become-weapons/a-79355073?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Road disputes are turning violent across India, raising questions about status and impunity behind the wheel for drivers of expensive cars.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan says strikes in Afghanistan killed '28 terrorists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09b8f54eb2ea48a16acad8801fec87c04e7f273c65e815c324a1420de089255e</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-says-strikes-in-afghanistan-killed-28-terrorists/a-79350604--4ba1c7a65a78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-says-strikes-in-afghanistan-killed-28-terrorists/a-79350604?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan border provinces of Kunar and Paktika were struck overnight. Pakistan said 28 militants were killed, Afghanistan said three civilians died. This follows soon after an attack on police in Kohat, Pakistan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: India's medal tally at Asian games rises to six</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f5e5e99df0de1fc0840dd46606495a7ae24e1972b4d6ab5c86b9d7f39cf71a0</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-s-medal-tally-at-asian-games-rises-to-six/live-79349941--4d2d3c9006df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-s-medal-tally-at-asian-games-rises-to-six/live-79349941?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian athletes won two bronze and two silver medals on the second day of the Asian Games in Japan. Meanwhile, more bodies were recovered after a flash flood in Kerala. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan: Typhoon Dujuan sparks flood, landslide warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3d280466afde9ec13dee69d594b8769524a5f457681cf4d90374e6bd8e36dff</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-typhoon-dujuan-sparks-flood-landslide-warnings/a-79349957--3d9e26ef9a38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-typhoon-dujuan-sparks-flood-landslide-warnings/a-79349957?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Evacuation advisories have been issued and hundreds of flights have been canceled in Japan, which is in the middle of a five-day holiday. The storm could dump record levels of rain on the country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec7ae787263e7fdc3e5f4e61d678d47165a02c77f8b16636f762326f453e94b1</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb848ac0da373b91748348ad8b978bfd759e25f87f69d26ec151f735c634a7fd</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e81e74728d90b5faf9d2e9c033fa1baa88f47718da94b132984b2adc434080a</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on amid war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:853fcaff81b8d4b87bdd560b80d93ab7ddc29d8f43c702cd34430a53a1fb50a6</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123--af9edc52c450.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
